cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, cite this project and the original datasets and backbones."
title: "POLAR Posture Recognition: Person-Centric Four- and Nine-Class Benchmarks"
type: software
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-22"
authors:
  - family-names: Huseyinli
    given-names: Abdulla
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdullahuseyinli-dot/polar-posture-recognition"
url: "https://github.com/abdullahuseyinli-dot/polar-posture-recognition"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Source-overlap-audited four- and nine-class POLAR posture classification with
  DINOv2, DINOv3, SigLIP2 and ConvNeXt V2. Development-nominated conservative
  fusions obtain 95.211019 and 94.583075 percent macro-F1 on 3,329 and 6,984 test
  images respectively. Prior models remain retained under the locked promotion
  rules. Includes public probabilities, audited membership, paired statistics,
  training code, technical reports and historical POLAR/V-COCO studies.
  The previously inspected four-class test is nested in the nine-class test;
  results do not establish an external state-of-the-art ranking.
keywords:
  - posture recognition
  - POLAR
  - DINOv2
  - DINOv3
  - ConvNeXt V2
  - SigLIP2
  - V-COCO
  - calibrated ensembles
  - source-overlap audit
  - reproducible evaluation
